Band Description

The Low Lantern Registry is a seven-member vocal-electronic ensemble built around the idea that low frequency can be passed from body to machine without losing communal scale.

**Gavino Carta** — lead voice, melodic contour, text, entry cues.
**Paolo Manca** — bassu, low throat resonance, pedal-tone control.
**Elia Piras** — contra, overtone bridge, rhythmic consonant attacks.
**Nico Sanna** — mesu boghe, upper support, harmonic locking.
**Lerato Mokoena** — kwaito drums, bass sequencing, live mutes, cassette-bus control.
**Marta Bellu** — prepared clavichord, tangent percussion, muted dyads, close-mic mechanical sound.
**Sipho Dlamini** — contrabass sarrusophone, breath pedals, split lows, key-click punctuation.

There is no conventional frontperson despite Gavino carrying many lead phrases. The ensemble treats the quartet as one shifting acoustic organism. Lerato structures the negative space around that organism, Marta provides tiny pitched attacks inside the gaps, and Sipho takes over low-register mass only when the vocal architecture makes room for him. Live performances avoid backing vocals, choir pads, and doubled lead tracks; every important vocal layer must originate from a person physically present in the formation.

